From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000005 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OrientCOMPASS <316423573+OrientCOMPASS@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Oct 2026 07:05:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] btif_av: sink CONNECT_REQ stays passive, PENDING open kept

Now that SEPs correctly advertise TSEP=SNK (0004-avdt), peers act as INT
and push SET_CONFIG to us.  The stock active BTA_AvOpen on CONNECT_REQ
races ahead of the peer (btsnoop: we SET_CONFIG 2.4 s before the Z40
opens signalling), marks our SEID in-use and the peer enters a
DISCOVER->ABORT loop.

Skip the INT open on CONNECT_REQ only.  The PENDING path keeps
BTA_AvOpen: it feeds bta_av_open_at_inc(), whose native collision logic
parks the request while the peer signals (coll_mask INC_TMR) and lets
the incoming SET_CONFIG win; accept_signalling_timer falls back to INT
if the peer stays silent.  (An earlier variant that also dropped the
PENDING open left lcb/rc half-built: bta_av_rc_create "ACP handle
exist" spam, ACL torn down locally, HCI reason 0x16.)
---
 btif/src/btif_av.c | 17 ++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/btif/src/btif_av.c b/btif/src/btif_av.c
index 03ba842..4d2c985 100644
--- a/btif/src/btif_av.c
+++ b/btif/src/btif_av.c
@@ -330,8 +330,23 @@ static BOOLEAN btif_av_state_idle_handler(btif_sm_event_t event, void *p_data)
              {
                  memcpy(&btif_av_cb.peer_bda, ((btif_av_connect_req_t*)p_data)->target_bda,
                                                                    sizeof(bt_bdaddr_t));
-                 BTA_AvOpen(btif_av_cb.peer_bda.address, btif_av_cb.bta_handle,
-                    TRUE, BTA_SEC_AUTHENTICATE, ((btif_av_connect_req_t*)p_data)->uuid);
+                 if (((btif_av_connect_req_t*)p_data)->uuid == UUID_SERVCLASS_AUDIO_SINK)
+                 {
+                     /* Passive sink on user-initiated connect: peers (phones,
+                      * Windows) act as INT and push SET_CONFIG to our SNK
+                      * SEPs.  Racing ahead as INT marks our SEID in-use and
+                      * the peer enters a DISCOVER->ABORT loop (btsnoop-proven
+                      * with Z40).  The PENDING path below still opens when the
+                      * peer's signalling arrives; open_at_inc() parks it while
+                      * the peer configures us, and accept_signalling_timer
+                      * falls back to INT if the peer stays silent. */
+                     APPL_TRACE_DEBUG("btif_av: sink connect - staying passive, peer will INT");
+                 }
+                 else
+                 {
+                     BTA_AvOpen(btif_av_cb.peer_bda.address, btif_av_cb.bta_handle,
+                        TRUE, BTA_SEC_AUTHENTICATE, ((btif_av_connect_req_t*)p_data)->uuid);
+                 }
              }
              else if (event == BTA_AV_PENDING_EVT)
              {
